{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing","id":840005,"title":"Is Chasing the Dragon still going to be a thing?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-01T10:29:23-08:00","id":840005,"title":"Is Chasing the Dragon still going to be a thing?","content":"Pardon me if I'm getting my nomenclature mixed up. <br /> <br /> By &quot;chasing the dragon&quot; I mean that unusual dragonblooded that pursues an Immaculate Martial Art that they are not elementally attuned to. A Fire Terrestrial pursuing Water Dragon style for instance. In 2nd Ed this and some added difficulties involved in it but once mastered gave some minor but cool benefits. <br /> <br /> In My Headcanon: when this was achieved it altered the essence of the Terrestrial making them vary unique cross elemental dragons Like the one mentioned above might be a Steam Dragon/Terrestrial, while a Water Terrestrial that chased the Fire Dragon might become a Boiling Dragon, etc... <br /> <br /> Do we have any information that this will still be a thing and will still be addressed? Or is this something I will likely have to reinsert into the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6473-raemus","name":"Raemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T10:46:56-08:00","id":840019,"title":"","content":"There is very little current information on Dragon-Blood interactions with Immaculate Martial Arts, and this term has not yet come up in the core book. We will likely have to wait for the DB book (4th book in the 