"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T12:20:16-08:00","id":840090,"title":"","content":"Begging the dragons I think is what you're looking for. I think it depends on if the out of aspect more aurcharge is making a comeback, from what I remember that was the benefit of mastering a style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T12:30:41-08:00","id":840101,"title":"","content":"Considering people totally hated the surcharge, I sure hope not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T12:34:16-08:00","id":840104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840101#post840101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering people totally hated the surcharge, I sure hope not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes I suspect if they had made it a discount instead of a surcharge people would have accepted it openly. Just make the baseline x motes higher by design and give an x mote discount for being properly aspected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T12:43:32-08:00","id":840109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840104#post840104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes I suspect if they had made it a discount instead of a surcharge people would have accepted it openly. Just make the baseline x motes higher by design and give an x mote discount for being properly aspected.</div> </div> </div> </div>The math would have been much more annoying - people generally find addition simpler and quicker than subtraction, and I've seen systems which use subtraction in its mechanics criticized because of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T12:44:43-08:00","id":840110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840104#post840104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sometimes I suspect if they had made it a discount instead of a surcharge people would have accepted it openly. Just make the baseline x motes higher by design and give an x mote discount for being properly aspected.</div> </div> </div> </div>People respond much better to this sort of game design; a perceived reward garners a better response than a perceived penalty, for obvious reasons.<br /> <br /> One of the classic examples of this is World of Warcraft. Back when they were designing it initially, in 2003, they were legitimately worried about people spending way to much time obsessively playing it. (This was back when Everquest was still a thing and was only somewhat jokingly known as &quot;Evercrack.&quot;) Initially, they came up with the idea of &quot;well, what if you gain XP normally for awhile, but after you've played for a certain amount of time you start earning it more slowly, to incentivize you doing something else for a bit?&quot;<br /> <br /> Playtesters hated that.<br /> <br /> Then they came up with the idea of &quot;Why don't we do the same thing, but we'll call the current fatigue state 'normal' and the current normal state 'rested.' People will feel like they're getting a bonus when they log on after a good nights sleep and are getting 'extra' XP for awhile because of it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Playtesters loved it even though it was the <i>exact same mechanic.</i><br /> <br /> Something I'd like to see, in addition to the idea of recasting the out-of-aspect &quot;penalties&quot; as bonuses instead, is for the Ability minimums to be framed as a bonus rather than an obligation. Instead of &quot;If you're playing a Dynast, you get X dots, but you MUST spend Y number of them on this ability spread&quot; it should be &quot;If you're playing a Dynast, you get Y number of dots in these Ability spreads FOR FREE! And you get Z dots to spend on whatever else you want&quot; where Z is actually X-Y. It's the precise same design, but framed in a much better way.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T12:52:32-08:00","id":840112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840109#post840109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The math would have been much more annoying - people generally find addition simpler and quicker than subtraction, and I've seen systems which use subtraction in its mechanics criticized because of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>While there's truth to that, the math would apply to fewer items. Instead of adding costs to 4 other aspects (not yours), you subtract costs from just 1 aspect (yours). So theoretically less work. But I was just going for perception. I guess it could go either way.<br /> <br /> In the end, though, I'd be fine with flat costs in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T12:53:34-08:00","id":840115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840104#post840104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sometimes I suspect if they had made it a discount instead of a surcharge people would have accepted it openly. Just make the baseline x motes higher by design and give an x mote discount for being properly aspected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually the math on that doesn't work, because what a lot of people, including me, often forget is that the mote surcharge applies once per tick. Which only works as a discount mechanic if DBs need to pay a mote to gain the ability to activate charms of that aspect, but that charge is waived if they're only activating charms for their own aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T12:54:14-08:00","id":840116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840110#post840110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the classic examples of this is World of Warcraft. Back when they were designing it initially, in 2003, they were legitimately worried about people spending way to much time obsessively playing it. (This was back when Everquest was still a thing and was only somewhat jokingly known as &quot;Evercrack.&quot;) Initially, they came up with the idea of &quot;well, what if you gain XP normally for awhile, but after you've played for a certain amount of time you start earning it more slowly, to incentivize you doing something else for a bit?&quot;<br /> <br /> Playtesters hated that.<br /> <br /> Then they came up with the idea of &quot;Why don't we do the same thing, but we'll call the current fatigue state 'normal' and the current normal state 'rested.' People will feel like they're getting a bonus when they log on after a good nights sleep and are getting 'extra' XP for awhile because of it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Playtesters loved it even though it was the <i>exact same mechanic.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I remember when that happened. It was hilarious, but even I couldn't deny it felt better than the other approach.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840110#post840110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I'd like to see, in addition to the idea of recasting the out-of-aspect &quot;penalties&quot; as bonuses instead, is for the Ability minimums to be framed as a bonus rather than an obligation. Instead of &quot;If you're playing a Dynast, you get X dots, but you MUST spend Y number of them on this ability spread&quot; it should be &quot;If you're playing a Dynast, you get Y number of dots in these Ability spreads FOR FREE! And you get Z dots to spend on whatever else you want&quot; where Z is actually X-Y. It's the precise same design, but framed in a much better way.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting idea!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T12:59:29-08:00","id":840119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I'd like to see, in addition to the idea of recasting the out-of-aspect &quot;penalties&quot; as bonuses instead, is for the Ability minimums to be framed as a bonus rather than an obligation. Instead of &quot;If you're playing a Dynast, you get X dots, but you MUST spend Y number of them on this ability spread&quot; it should be &quot;If you're playing a Dynast, you get Y number of dots in these Ability spreads FOR FREE! And you get Z dots to spend on whatever else you want&quot; where Z is actually X-Y. It's the precise same design, but framed in a much better way.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, that whole &quot;illusion of choice&quot; thing really bugs me in regards to DB and Sidereal Chargen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T13:10:15-08:00","id":840128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840119#post840119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah, that whole &quot;illusion of choice&quot; thing really bugs me in regards to DB and Sidereal Chargen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Illusion of Choice is great for Storytellers building plot. It doesn't work too well for players building characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T13:58:11-08:00","id":840153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840104#post840104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sometimes I suspect if they had made it a discount instead of a surcharge people would have accepted it openly. Just make the baseline x motes higher by design and give an x mote discount for being properly aspected.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually did this in my games and even allowed 0 cost charms (very rare except for first excellency) and it worked great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6473-raemus","name":"Raemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T13:59:12-08:00","id":840154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840090#post840090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Begging the dragons I think is what you're looking for. I think it depends on if the out of aspect more aurcharge is making a comeback, from what I remember that was the benefit of mastering a style.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks! I knew I was mixing up the nomenclature","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6473-raemus","name":"Raemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T14:11:32-08:00","id":840161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840112#post840112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While there's truth to that, the math would apply to fewer items. Instead of adding costs to 4 other aspects (not yours), you subtract costs from just 1 aspect (yours). So theoretically less work. But I was just going for perception. I guess it could go either way.<br /> <br /> In the end, though, I'd be fine with flat costs in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with that is I suspect you'd still end up doing more math than you'd like, since now the modification is to the charms you're using and buying most often.<br /> <br /> That said, the writers have given the impression they're weighing things out as they go, so I suspect the mechanics to encourage characters to play to their aspect may be different this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T14:21:22-08:00","id":840169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840104#post840104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sometimes I suspect if they had made it a discount instead of a surcharge people would have accepted it openly. Just make the baseline x motes higher by design and give an x mote discount for being properly aspected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or just don't? Make your interesting thematic statements in the narrative without mechanically punishing stuff a player might find fun? Maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T14:27:38-08:00","id":840176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840119#post840119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah, that whole &amp;quot;illusion of choice&amp;quot; thing really bugs me in regards to DB and Sidereal Chargen.</div> </div> </div> </div>But don't we kind of get that same illusion of choice with the new Solar Caste Abilities? Except for Dawn, I think every Caste has at least two abilities that are kind of necessary for it to fulfill it's Caste Role Bonus. Zenith is Presence/Performance and Resistance, Twilights are Lore and Occult, Nights are Stealth and Larceny, and Eclipses are Socialize and Ride/Sail. Theoretically you could make characters without those abilities as Caste abilities but they would be pretty terrible at their roles. So wouldn't it be easier to offer that kind of idea with Dynastic abilities, like here's some abilities that due to your dynastic heritage, you might have as favored or Caste abilities and then overlay those with the caste ability choices for characters? (Assuming DB's get the same choice mechanic for their caste abilities.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T14:42:55-08:00","id":840184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840169#post840169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or just don't? Make your interesting thematic statements in the narrative without mechanically punishing stuff a player might find fun? Maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's crazy-talk! Everyone knows that tabletop RPG players are masochists and love punishing mechanics! Interesting narrative is for communists!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T15:14:13-08:00","id":840199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840104#post840104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sometimes I suspect if they had made it a discount instead of a surcharge people would have accepted it openly. Just make the baseline x motes higher by design and give an x mote discount for being properly aspected.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are right. It's a reward versus punishment thing. People would much rather feel rewarded for playing 'in aspect' than punished for playing out of aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T17:30:54-08:00","id":840278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840169#post840169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or just don't? Make your interesting thematic statements in the narrative without mechanically punishing stuff a player might find fun? Maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>But part of the fun can come from restrictions! Especially considering that DBs are the polar opposite to Solars in that regard. Sidereals are also like this, to a lesser extent. They've got really restrictive charmsets and even their fluff has a bunch of obstacles you've got to get around. They're weighted with responsibility, oftentimes from many places, and they need to balance that against eachother and their own personal wants and values. <br /> <br /> For Sidereals, their charms are powerful, but not broad in scope and can't be added onto with your own custom charms. For DBs they're really pulled into their aspect, to the point where it affects their personalities. You can absolutely be a wood aspect melee fighter, but you're going to struggle just a bit more than a fire aspect to do it. It's not much, just a little extra push of essence every time you use it to enhance your sword, but it's there. You have to come to terms with the fact that you're struggling against the blood of Sextes Jylis, and that it's a slightly uphill battle.<br /> <br /> It's represented mechanically because sometimes fluff and mechanics are tied together. Solars are the most powerful so they get the most powerful charms, Sidereals are strange fate ninjas so their charms do odd, powerful and sneaky things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T17:52:58-08:00","id":840287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840104#post840104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes I suspect if they had made it a discount instead of a surcharge people would have accepted it openly. Just make the baseline x motes higher by design and give an x mote discount for being properly aspected.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I usually feel, giving something extra rather than taking something away is always more palatable to me even if they boil down to the same result. I would say this rule could (should?) have been applied to EX3 Martial Arts too by having them start at &quot;terrestrial&quot; as the base charm with added tiers for &quot;celestial mastery&quot; and &quot;solar mastery&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840278#post840278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But part of the fun can come from restrictions! Especially considering that DBs are the polar opposite to Solars in that regard. Sidereals are also like this, to a lesser extent. They've got really restrictive charmsets and even their fluff has a bunch of obstacles you've got to get around. They're weighted with responsibility, oftentimes from many places, and they need to balance that against eachother and their own personal wants and values.<br /> <br /> For Sidereals, their charms are powerful, but not broad in scope and can't be added onto with your own custom charms. For DBs they're really pulled into their aspect, to the point where it affects their personalities. You can absolutely be a wood aspect melee fighter, but you're going to struggle just a bit more than a fire aspect to do it. It's not much, just a little extra push of essence every time you use it to enhance your sword, but it's there. You have to come to terms with the fact that you're struggling against the blood of Sextes Jylis, and that it's a slightly uphill battle.<br /> <br /> It's represented mechanically because sometimes fluff and mechanics are tied together. Solars are the most powerful so they get the most powerful charms, Sidereals are strange fate ninjas so their charms do odd, powerful and sneaky things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if base mote costs are the place to represent a DB's elemental mastery/purview in the first place. I think I would prefer to see charms with some added effect that that is activated either by paying more motes/wp/init/whatever <b>OR</b> being the right aspect. A Wood Aspect can use Melee charms but to get the full incendiary potential of those inherently Fire Aspected charms it will cost more motes.<br /> <br /> This might not even be a issue anymore as I feel like at one point it was suggested that the DB charmset was going to have a lot more elemental overlap and include more charms that had flavour fitting to all aspects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T18:51:18-08:00","id":840311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheGraySoul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840176#post840176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But don't we kind of get that same illusion of choice with the new Solar Caste Abilities? Except for Dawn, I think every Caste has at least two abilities that are kind of necessary for it to fulfill it's Caste Role Bonus. Zenith is Presence/Performance and Resistance, Twilights are Lore and Occult, Nights are Stealth and Larceny, and Eclipses are Socialize and Ride/Sail. Theoretically you could make characters without those abilities as Caste abilities but they would be pretty terrible at their roles. So wouldn't it be easier to offer that kind of idea with Dynastic abilities, like here's some abilities that due to your dynastic heritage, you might have as favored or Caste abilities and then overlay those with the caste ability choices for characters? (Assuming DB's get the same choice mechanic for their caste abilities.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really agree with that. Playing a roguish face could easily be an Eclipse without Ride or Sail. I'd happily play a Twilight without Lore (for example, a barbarian shaman). In a game some of my friends play, the Zenith is a man of the wilds, focused on Athletics, Resistance and Survival, I think he doesn't have Performance or Presence.<br /> Not sure I can think of a Night concept with no Stealth or Larceny... maybe a detective? Awareness, Investigation, Socialise... I'd imagine you'd take Larceny for understanding crime though.<br /> <br /> Anyway, certainly the stereotypical version of that caste will always take those abilities (except maybe the Eclipse: I'm not sure, but I think the Eclipse face-character in my game might not have Ride or Sail). But you don't have to be a stereotype.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, on the surcharge. Whether it's a discount or addition, I don't want it, because players will constantly forget about it, and maths already slows down a lot of players.<br /> Frankly, the fact that it costs less xp, combined with the fact that you always get your elemental version first (especially if they have more elemental charms this time) is definitely enough (I mean, if you're an Air Aspect and you buy Dragon-Graced Weapon, you get a lightning blade not a fire blade first) is enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T19:42:33-08:00","id":840338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840104#post840104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes I suspect if they had made it a discount instead of a surcharge people would have accepted it openly. Just make the baseline x motes higher by design and give an x mote discount for being properly aspected.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with this is that it would make every single DB charm look overcosted at first glance, since they would all be listed with an increased mote cost that most players are not intended to pay. It would also straightforwardly add more math and tracking to the game, because (again) the assumption is that DBs are mostly using in-aspect charms -- requiring that people remember the +1 mote cost for the occasional out-of-aspect charm makes much more sense than requiring that they remember the -1 discount for nearly every charm they use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 03-01-2016, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T20:01:15-08:00","id":840346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840287#post840287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if base mote costs are the place to represent a DB's elemental mastery/purview in the first place. I think I would prefer to see charms with some added effect that that is activated either by paying more motes/wp/init/whatever <b>OR</b> being the right aspect. A Wood Aspect can use Melee charms but to get the full incendiary potential of those inherently Fire Aspected charms it will cost more motes.<br /> <br /> This might not even be a issue anymore as I feel like at one point it was suggested that the DB charmset was going to have a lot more elemental overlap and include more charms that had flavour fitting to all aspects.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could be cool, like they did with MA charms and the terrestrial/mastery keyword.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T20:33:56-08:00","id":840358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840346#post840346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That could be cool, like they did with MA charms and the terrestrial/mastery keyword.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did some theorizing in that direction <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/814402-db-theorizing-aspect-keyword\">a while back</a>. It's a great idea that I hope they do some version of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T21:58:31-08:00","id":840398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840110#post840110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of &quot;If you're playing a Dynast, you get X dots, but you MUST spend Y number of them on this ability spread&quot; it should be &quot;If you're playing a Dynast, you get Y number of dots in these Ability spreads FOR FREE! And you get Z dots to spend on whatever else you want&quot; where Z is actually X-Y. It's the precise same design, but framed in a much better way.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, from a player-usability standpoint, is such a huge thing. Friggin' Sidereal chargen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T22:15:49-08:00","id":840406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840311#post840311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't really agree with that. Playing a roguish face could easily be an Eclipse without Ride or Sail. I'd happily play a Twilight without Lore (for example, a barbarian shaman). In a game some of my friends play, the Zenith is a man of the wilds, focused on Athletics, Resistance and Survival, I think he doesn't have Performance or Presence.<br /> Not sure I can think of a Night concept with no Stealth or Larceny... maybe a detective? Awareness, Investigation, Socialise... I'd imagine you'd take Larceny for understanding crime though.<br /> <br /> Anyway, certainly the stereotypical version of that caste will always take those abilities (except maybe the Eclipse: I'm not sure, but I think the Eclipse face-character in my game might not have Ride or Sail). But you don't have to be a stereotype.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if you notice, I did say Resistance for Zeniths. :P<br /> And I was referring to the role bonuses for each Caste, wherein the Eclipse gets a role bonus to experience for overcoming geographical problems for the group, the Twilight gets a bonus for solving a problem through knowledge or education, Nights for anything sneaky and underhanded, and Zeniths for inspiring others.<br /> <br /> But this is just kind of semantics. I think I like Murcushio's suggestion the best so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T22:25:49-08:00","id":840415,"title":"","content":"I thought &quot;Chasing the Dragon&quot; was <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:chasing-the-dragon\" target=\"_blank\">a term for when DBs sequester themselves from the world in order to train up their Essence score</a>. I mean, that's how I used it in that post, and I hadn't seen it used for other stuff beforehand, I think.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure it's a thing this edition, to be honest. Like, I think it is, but PCs get an exemption? I could be wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 03-02-2016, 01:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T22:33:52-08:00","id":840418,"title":"","content":"To be quite honest, the out-of-caste mote surcharge seems much more palatable in an edition where Dragonblooded might have the Listed 8, Pick 5 caste/aspect abilities Solars do. It always bothered me that (ignoring how weird the actual charmsets were) that Fire Caste got the seemingly &quot;best&quot; spread of aspect abilities, what with getting Dodge, Melee, Socialize, Presence, and Athletics. That's a Dawns wet-dream caste-charm list, if you ask me, and no one should have got a spread that good in an edition of 5 and only 5 caste/aspect abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","name":"Grindavikur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T22:57:21-08:00","id":840424,"title":"","content":"Fire Aspects were definitely one of the most popular (possibly the most popular) aspect I saw played (with Air second, then Water, then Air, with Earth definitely at the bottom, probably because they had no real combat ability).<br /> Not just because of their good spread (I mean, I think people just thought shooting fire and fighting while on fire is awesome), but that's part of it. I mean, if you thought &quot;I'll play a social/combat character&quot;, Fire Aspects have the most obviously useful set of abilities. Air was generally spies and sorcerers; Water for spies, pirates or martial artists; Wood either wilderness archers or Cynis decadents; Earth hardly ever appeared.<br /> It didn't help that Melee and Dodge happened to more powerful than, say, Resistance or Archery. I mean, you should have been able to go &quot;I'll play a guy who focuses on being really tough in combat, so I'll play an Earth&quot; but in practice you weren't that good.<br /> <br /> I still wouldn't want the out-of-aspect charge even if it covers more, because it's still maths that players will continually forget.<br /> I'm certainly not going to bother using it for the NPCs when I run a 3rd ed combat against the Wyld Hunt in this week's session.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T02:41:25-08:00","id":840501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840424#post840424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Earth hardly ever appeared.</div> </div> </div> </div>I found that when Earth aspects appeared it's because they took the entire War tree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T03:22:03-08:00","id":840528,"title":"","content":"That doesn't surprise me.<br /> We already had an Air Aspect general in our main game (as back in 1st ed, you used Lore for warfare, and it made sense for a Tepet), and the Fire Aspect soldiers took War anyway, so as war charms didn't come up that much, we never saw an Earth general.<br /> Once we had an Earth aspect architect, but the player didn't stay in the game for that long.<br /> In another game, we had a Mnemon earth aspect, he had loads of jewellery and a massive hammer. His concept was &quot;Mnemon's favourite grandson&quot; so of course he was Earth-Aspected. If Mnemon was a different aspect though, he'd have just been that. I don't think being Earth aspected was really important to his character, though he did use Craft charms (to make statues of Mnemon).<br /> I did have fun accusing him of being like the Ostenatious Peasant (antithesis of Pasiap) though, with all his bling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T08:00:03-08:00","id":840658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840501#post840501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I found that when Earth aspects appeared it's because they took the entire War tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or they were an Immaculate and wanted to get some of that sweet sweet Grand Goremaul action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T08:00:49-08:00","id":840659,"title":"","content":"It would be remiss of me, in a thread with this title that hasn't yet mentioned them .... that DBs can &quot;Chase the dragon&quot; with the opiates from the Beasts of Resplendent Virtue; a.k.a Crack pissing dino pets.<br /> <br /> I do so hope they're back in 3E!<br /> <br /> Anyway ... I'll get my coat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/907-jay","name":"Jay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T08:33:03-08:00","id":840675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840658#post840658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or they were an Immaculate and wanted to get some of that sweet sweet Grand Goremaul action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or if the player had read Scroll of the Monk, regular Goremaul/wrestling action, as Jade Mountain style was one of the best ones.<br /> Though... you still had to pay the mote surcharge on Martial Arts excellencies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T10:23:18-08:00","id":840756,"title":"","content":"I think Earth Aspects showed up more than twice as often as any other Aspect out there... and possibly as much as all other DB appearances combined! In my games, that is. Something I just love about them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T18:01:34-08:00","id":841037,"title":"","content":"Really? We hardly ever saw them. I guess it just depends on the group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T19:49:38-08:00","id":841069,"title":"","content":"It's Beasts of Resplendent <i>Liquid</i>. If they could piss Virtue dots I think a lot more players would have taken them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T21:38:54-08:00","id":841121,"title":"","content":"Well, that depends on the virtue. If it was Conviction, absolutely. If Compassion, depends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T05:00:30-08:00","id":841228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=840278#post840278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But part of the fun can come from restrictions! Especially considering that DBs are the polar opposite to Solars in that regard. Sidereals are also like this, to a lesser extent. They've got really restrictive charmsets and even their fluff has a bunch of obstacles you've got to get around. They're weighted with responsibility, oftentimes from many places, and they need to balance that against eachother and their own personal wants and values. <br /> <br /> For Sidereals, their charms are powerful, but not broad in scope and can't be added onto with your own custom charms. For DBs they're really pulled into their aspect, to the point where it affects their personalities. You can absolutely be a wood aspect melee fighter, but you're going to struggle just a bit more than a fire aspect to do it. It's not much, just a little extra push of essence every time you use it to enhance your sword, but it's there. You have to come to terms with the fact that you're struggling against the blood of Sextes Jylis, and that it's a slightly uphill battle.<br /> <br /> It's represented mechanically because sometimes fluff and mechanics are tied together. Solars are the most powerful so they get the most powerful charms, Sidereals are strange fate ninjas so their charms do odd, powerful and sneaky things.</div> </div> </div> </div>why exactly does it need to be this way? What's the value in having a player who wants to be a Wood Aspect swordsman suck a mechanical penalty every time he wants to use Melee charms? I agree with SpruceStripedGoose. Better to have specific elemental weird flair things than take a mechanical dump on a concept which is what the out of aspect surcharge does. <br /> <br /> Sometimes mechanics and fluff are tied together, sure. Not always successfully. Sids' closed Charmset accomplishes this much better than the surcharge or something like formlock. The closed Charmset encourages creative Charm use. Formlock and the surcharge encourage one true builds or limited options in a way that don't actually benefit creativity. What value do they actually create for the DB play experience? I can't think of one, unlike what the closed Charmset does for Sids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T03:19:56-08:00","id":841801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/840005-is-chasing-the-dragon-still-going-to-be-a-thing?p=841069#post841069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's Beasts of Resplendent <i>Liquid</i>. If they could piss Virtue dots I think a lot more players would have taken them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gah. My bad. Quite right.<br /> <br /> Though a pint of narcotic Compassion would be a rather decadent for a Dynastic soiree me thinks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/907-jay","name":"Jay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}